+
+# Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901). Export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`.
+It returns the value the pointer refers to, and throws an error when the pointer is not a valid JSON
+Pointer or does not resolve to a value of the document. Later features build on it.
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- "" returns the whole document; "/a/b" walks object members; array indices are decimal without leading zeros.
+- `~1` decodes to `/` and `~0` to `~` (in that order); any other `~` escape is invalid.
+- A non-empty pointer not starting with "/" is invalid.
+- Missing members, out-of-range indices, "-" and non-canonical indices, and stepping into primitives throw.
+- Only own properties resolve (no `__proto__`, `constructor`, prototype members).
diff --git a/src/index.ts b/src/index.ts
